# XSH thrd_yield()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The page fixes no observable effect beyond returning; the test
# checks that repeated calls return and leave the other thread able to run.

assertion  XSH.thrd_yield.001
anchor     functions/thrd_yield.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A thread calling thrd_yield() repeatedly (1000 times) gets control
           back each time, while another thread, started meanwhile, runs and
           sets a flag that the yielding thread sees within 10 s.
test       t/001-returns.c
